1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,700
The six-carbon sugar then splits into two three-carbon pieces.

2
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:13,111
Each is oxidised, handing hydrogen to NAD plus to make NADH, and each yields two ATP directly.

3
00:00:13,111 --> 00:00:19,270
Making ATP this way, straight from a substrate, is substrate-level phosphorylation.

